# Minimal-root generation of the @:dataClass resident-emission probe.
#
# The entry list holds exactly ONE root: the @:dataClass class whose generated
# comparator calls into the resident runtime.SortedTable. No sorted map or set
# value exists in the program, so the std.SortedMap* keys are never lit by the
# type cases -- only the requireType bridge in RustImports can gate
# runtime.SortedTable in.
#
# This root set is the point: on the full corpus the emission gate is a global
# union over one shared shimsUsed map, so any unrelated module lighting those
# keys keeps sorted_table.rs emitted and hides the bridge's absence. (PIT-390)
#
# Run from the repository root; the runner records rc and the raw log.
-lib reflaxe
-lib boring
-cp packages/compiler
-cp packages/compiler/reflaxe/rust/std-shadow
-cp packages/compiler/reflaxe/rust
-cp samples
--macro Intercept.run(['samples'])
--macro rustcompiler.Compiler.use()
-D rust-output=out/rust-resident-dataclass/gen
-D runtime-import=crate::runtime
-D runtime-emit=runtime
boring.DataClassStringCompare
